  "section_notes": "The final text keeps a 55 °C test with a 5% permanent cap and an immediate sales stop, which blocks the Hearth 10 (6.2%) until remediation. The recall trigger is 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which applies directly to the Ember 8 (9.9). The retrofit window of six years favours Northwind's remote shut-off gap, and the 36-month suppression delay favours Halcyon's costs, so each company is hit on one flagship and gains on one cost-related item."
